            // The proxy bytecode is well-known for ERC1967Factory.

            // From the initCode in ERC1967FactoryConstants and the BYTECODE,
            // I can extract the proxy runtime code by analyzing the _initCode function.

            // The proxy deployed by ERC1967Factory has this runtime code:
            // (This is the standard ERC1967Factory transparent proxy runtime)

            // Let me construct it properly based on the function signatures and patterns.

            // Proxy Runtime Code:
            // ====================
            // The proxy stores implementation at ERC1967 implementation slot.
            // If msg.sender == factory:
